## Mitigations

- Disable WebDAV when it is not required.
- Restrict unnecessary HTTP methods such as `PUT` and `DELETE`.
- Disable directory listing.
- Never store plaintext credentials in web-accessible files.
- Restrict access to backup and configuration files.
- Apply least-privilege permissions to WebDAV directories.
- Prevent uploaded files from being executed as server-side code.
- Remove unnecessary IIS functionality.
- Monitor IIS logs for suspicious HTTP methods and file uploads.
- Rotate credentials immediately if they become exposed.

